{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"MXLPosition","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y attributes change the computation of the default position. For most elements, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"origin is changed relative to the left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the bar (x) and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the top line of the staff (y)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the following elements, the default-x value changes the origin relative to the start of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"note - figured-bass - harmony - link - directive - measure-numbering - all descendants of the part-list"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element - all children of the direction-type element"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This origin is from the start of the entire measure, at either the left barline or the start of the system."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the default-x attribute is used within a child element of the part-name-display, part-abbreviation-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display, group-name-display, or group-abbreviation-display elements, it changes the origin relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the first measure on the system. These values are used when the current measure or a succeeding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure starts a new system. The same change of origin is used for the group-symbol element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the note, figured-bass, and harmony elements, the default-x value is considered to have adjusted the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"musical position within the bar for its descendant elements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the credit-words and credit-image elements are not related to a measure, in these cases the default-x"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and default-y attributes adjust the origin relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the specified page."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The relative-x and relative-y attributes change the position relative to the default position, either as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"computed by the individual program, or as overridden by the default-x and default-y attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive x is right, negative x is left; positive y is up, negative y is down. All units are in tenths of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interline space. For stems, positive relative-y lengthens a stem while negative relative-y shortens it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y position attributes provide higher-resolution positioning data than related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features such as the placement attribute and the offset element. Applications reading a MusicXML file that can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understand both features should generally rely on the default-x and default-y attributes for their greater"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accuracy. For the relative-x and relative-y attributes, the offset element, placement attribute, and directive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute provide context for the relative position information, so the two features should be interpreted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As elsewhere in the MusicXML format, tenths are the global tenths defined by the scaling element, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local tenths of a staff resized by the staff-size element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLPosition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"defaultX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"defaultY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"relativeX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"relativeY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"title":"init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/init(defaultx:defaulty:relativex:relativey:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/defaultX":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/defaultx","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The default horizontal position, in tenths, changing the computation of the default position relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the measure."}],"title":"defaultX","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultX","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/relativeY":{"title":"relativeY","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/relativey","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The vertical position, in tenths, relative to the default position, either as computed by the application or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as overridden by ","type":"text"},{"code":"defaultY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Positive values are up, negative values down; for stems, a positive value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lengthens the stem while a negative value shortens it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"relativeY"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXL